<p><img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Dome_of_Cattedrale_di_Santa_Maria_del_Fiore_%28Florence%29.jpg/2560px-Dome_of_Cattedrale_di_Santa_Maria_del_Fiore_%28Florence%29.jpg" alt="img" /></p>
<p>The other day on twitter, I saw the question posed: <em>“What are your favourite drugs/escapes from reality?”</em></p>
<p>After going down that path in my 20s and finding no reprieve, I would say to my friend that asked the question: <strong>the goal is not to escape reality, but to align with it - to push toward reality with all your might.</strong></p>
<p>Now, you might be saying “but Josh, the world is so bleak, there’s so much evil in it - I don’t want to live here, I want escape!”</p>
<p><strong>Yes.</strong></p>
<p>Hear me out: you feel this way because this world is <strong>NOT</strong> <em>reality</em>.</p>
<p>We live in the <em>fallen shadow of reality</em>.</p>
<p>Let me remind you: <strong>You are an infinite soul in a body that was meant to live forever - this is not home</strong>.</p>
<p>It’s why most of us look around on many days and think of the world around us as a strange place.
There is certainly beauty and goodness to behold, but it’s a strange imperfect place.</p>
<p>Now, don’t start to think that the world is illusion (Gnosticism) - it is incomplete and imperfect because of <em>us</em>, because of <em>our fallen nature</em>, because <em>sin</em>.
I had previously made the mistake in believing that this world is “not real” - not so.
Matter is real, it “matters” (pun intended) - the reason so many people <em>worship nature and the Creation itself rather than the Creator</em> is that Creation <em>really is</em> Good.</p>
<p>The reason that Christ came as a man, as the Word incarnate, because matter is Real. God doesn’t despise matter - on the contrary He assumed it - forever uniting divinity and flesh.</p>
<p><strong>God is reality itself.</strong></p>
<p>Find God, and you find <strong>Truth</strong>, you find what <strong>actually is.</strong></p>
<p>From there, all joy and peace is to be lived, for that is grasping Heaven.</p>
<p>Heaven is not “somewhere else” - it is not yet fully realized for us, but it is “already - not yet”.</p>
<p>So, your goal, the goal of everyone here and now is to cooperate with Christ in the redemption of Reality.</p>
<p>You are playing eternal games whether you know it or not.
There is an eternal ascent toward Reality itself, the ultimate journey is at hand.
Not an “abstract ascent” - but a very Real one in a life of Prayer, in the Sacraments which pierce the veil and break into the here and now.</p>
<p>Go all in on reality, these is no such thing as “escape”.</p>
<p>As always, God bless, and until next time.</p>
